            "Title": "Security groups should not allow ingress from 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 to port 22",
            "Description": "This control checks whether an Amazon EC2 security group allows ingress from ‘0.0.0.0/0’ or ‘::/0’ to port 22. The control fails if the security group allows ingress from ‘0.0.0.0/0’ or ‘::/0’ to port 22.",
            "Remediation": {
                "Recommendation": {
                    "Text": "To prohibit ingress to port 22, remove the rule that allows such access for each security group associated with a VPC. For instructions, see \"Update security group rules\" in the Amazon EC2 User Guide. After selecting a security group in the Amazon EC2 console, choose Actions, Edit inbound rules. Remove the rule that allows access to port 22.",
                    "Url": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/working-with-security-group-rules.html"
                }
            },
